# Events on the Old Svalich Road west of Vallaki, toward Krezk (data/random_encounters/krezk_road.json).

~ belview_cart
set clovin_met_on_road
Narrator: A handcart lies tipped in the ditch with one wheel off. Beside it, sitting on an empty wine cask, is a stooped figure in a monk's cast-off habit, with one ear like a hound's and a hand that is mostly feathers.
Clovin Belview: Don't. Don't say it. I know what I look like. I look like a man who walked two days to a winery and found nobody to sell him wine. That's what I look like.
* What happened at the winery? -> winery
* [Athletics DC 10] Let us put your wheel back on. -> wheel_ok | wheel_fail
* We'll leave you to it. -> END

~ winery
Clovin Belview: Trouble, they said. Didn't open the gate, didn't sell me a drop. Somebody shouted from a window to go home, there was trouble, and to tell everyone. So. I'm telling everyone. You're everyone.
Clovin Belview: The Abbot will be disappointed. He doesn't shout when he's disappointed. He just gets very kind. You don't want him kind.
-> END

~ wheel_ok
set clovin_befriended
Narrator: The wheel goes back on its axle with a clunk, and the little cart rights itself. Clovin looks at it, and at you, as if nobody has ever done anything for him on purpose.
Clovin Belview: Well. Well, now. Clovin Belview, of the Abbey of St. Markovia, up over Krezk. If you're ever that way, I'll pour you something. If there's ever anything to pour.
-> END

~ wheel_fail
Narrator: The wheel slides off the axle twice, the second time onto a foot. Clovin watches with the air of a man whose day could not, in fact, get worse, and has just been proved wrong.
Clovin Belview: Leave it. I'll carry it. I carry everything else.
-> END

~ waystone
Narrator: At a bend stands a waist-high stone with a sunburst cut into it, so old the rays are just dents. A candle burns in a niche at its foot, though there's no one in sight.
* Leave a coin for whoever keeps it lit. -> waystone_coin
* Walk on. -> END

~ waystone_coin
gold -1
Narrator: The coin clicks into the niche beside the candle. The flame doesn't move, but for a mile after, the wind seems to be at your backs.
interject tag:pious: The White Sun's people. Krezk's not far, then.
-> END
